Chromium WebUI: TrustedHTML DOM type augmentation for TypeScript 7+.

Origin: EmberBSD, not submitted upstream.
Source: Chromium ui/webui and tools/typescript under EmberBSD.
Apply after gn-shared-node-providers.patch.

TypeScript 7+ ships lib.dom.d.ts where Element.innerHTML is string-only.
Chromium's update_npm_deps patches the bundled TypeScript's lib.dom to
widen innerHTML/outerHTML setters for TrustedHTML; when using the host
TypeScript those patches are absent.  Add a standalone global ambient
augmentation that TypeScript merges during compilation, and reference it
from static_types.ts so every WebUI ts_library target inherits the fix.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/ui/webui/resources/js/trusted_types_dom_compat.d.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+// Copyright 2026 The Chromium Authors
+// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license that can be
+// found in the LICENSE file.
+
+// TypeScript 7+ narrows Element.innerHTML / ShadowRoot.innerHTML to
+// string in lib.dom.d.ts.  Chromium WebUI assigns TrustedHTML values
+// (emptyHTML(), sanitizeInnerHtml()) for Trusted Types CSP compliance.
+// Widen the property declarations so those assignments type-check.
+
+interface Element {
+  innerHTML: string | TrustedHTML;
+}
+
+interface ShadowRoot {
+  innerHTML: string | TrustedHTML;
+}
--- a/ui/webui/resources/js/static_types.ts
+++ b/ui/webui/resources/js/static_types.ts
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
+/// <reference path="trusted_types_dom_compat.d.ts" />
 // Copyright 2024 The Chromium Authors
 // Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license that can be
 // found in the LICENSE file.
